version: treat any non-negative uname() return as success

POSIX specifies that uname() returns a non-negative value on success, and
illumos returns 1, so the check in get_uname_info() reports every call as a
failure there, with a stale errno:

  agent=git/2.54.0-uname().failed.with.error.'No.such.file.or.directory'.(2)

Test for a negative return, as dir.c already does.

--- a/version.c	2026-09-22 17:43:02.490369702 -0400
+++ b/version.c	2026-09-22 17:43:03.429402194 -0400
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@
 {
 	struct utsname uname_info;
 
-	if (uname(&uname_info)) {
+	if (uname(&uname_info) < 0) {
 		strbuf_addf(buf, _("uname() failed with error '%s' (%d)\n"),
 			    strerror(errno),
 			    errno);
